      "result": {
        "reply_text": "you paid for mixer repair but the service was never provided and you have not taken any action yet.\n\na complaint to the District Commission must be filed within two years from the date on which the cause of action has arisen, unless the commission permits a delay for sufficient cause.\n\nthe District Commission has jurisdiction to entertain complaints where the value of goods or services paid as consideration does not exceed one crore rupees.\n\nyou can file a complaint with the District Commission.\n\ngather all your receipts, bills, and any messages or written records you have with the repair shop.\n\nconsult a lawyer to check if your delay can be condoned and to help file your complaint before the District Commission.\n\ndo you have any written receipt or proof of payment showing the amount paid to the shop?\n\ndo you have any chat messages, call logs, or written communication with the repair shop about the unprovided service?\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 69\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 34\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
